<newsitem itemid="62645" id="root" date="1996-09-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Next first half profits rise to 56 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Next first half profits rise to 56 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to July 27</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		10.9		   vs 8.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.0		    vs 3.75</p>
<p> Pretax		     56.0		   vs 50.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   406.4		  vs 333.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 53.0 to 55.0 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 49.8		   vs 37.9</p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs 6.0 gain</p>
<p> Interest receivable    6.2		    vs 6.2</p>
<p> Tax			  15.1		   vs 12.8</p>
<p> Net taxed		  40.9		   vs 37.3</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 2 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  December 3</p>
<p> Ex-div date		November 25</p>
<p>NOTE - Retailer Next Plc said trading profits before tax of 56.0 million stg compare with 44.1 million, which excludes a six million stg exceptional gain on a disposal last year.</p>
</text>
